<title>FINLAND: ERM link will not change Finland monetary policy.</title>
<headline>ERM link will not change Finland monetary policy.</headline>
<dateline>HELSINKI 1996-10-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bank of Finland governor Sirkka Hamalainen told a news conference on Saturday the central bank's monetary policy would be unchanged after the markka had been linked to Europe's exchange rate mechanism.</p>
<p>&quot;This means a continuation of exactly the same monetary policy line,&quot; she told reporters, explaining that all ERM member countries have, &quot;explicitly or implicitly&quot;, had the same target for low inflation as the Bank of Finland.</p>
<p>Finland and the European Union monetary committee earlier agreed to peg the markka to Europe's Exchange Rate Mechanism.</p>
<p>-- Helsinki newsroom +35 80 6805 0247</p>
</text>
